# Agent Behavior Rules
- Never leave incomplete code, placeholder comments (`// TODO`), or `...` in your output. Always provide complete, copy-pasteable implementations.
- Before modifying more than 3 files or starting a complex refactor, you must write a step-by-step plan and wait for my approval.
- Do not invent or assume the existence of npm packages. If you need a new dependency, ask for permission first.
- When fixing TypeScript errors, strictly ban the use of `@ts-ignore` or `any`. Use `unknown` with type narrowing instead.